The test `['org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.ArchiveStreamFactoryTest.shortTextFilesAreNoTARs()']` failed.
The test looks like:

```java
31 :     @Test
32 :     public void shortTextFilesAreNoTARs() throws Exception {
33 :         try {
34 :             new ArchiveStreamFactory()
35 :                 .createArchiveInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream("This certainly is not a tar archive, really, no kidding".getBytes()));
36 :             fail("created an input stream for a non-archive");
37 :         } catch (ArchiveException ae) {
38 :             assertTrue(ae.getMessage().startsWith("No Archiver found"));
39 :         }
40 :     }
```

Current bug report: {'summary': 'createArchiveInputStream detects text files less than 100 bytes as tar archives', 'description': 'The fix for [](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/COMPRESS-117 "Certain tar files not recognised by ArchiveStreamFactory") which modified ArchiveStreamFactory().createArchiveInputStream(inputstream) results in short text files (empirically seems to be those <= 100 bytes) being detected as tar archives which obviously is not desirable if one wants to know whether or not the files are archives.  '}

Proceed to fault localisation and produce a step-by-step diagnosis.

